;; repr/clojure's round trips (bin/repr-clojure check --roundtrip, doc/REPR-CLOJURE.md, "Print"):
;; the files that do not come back byte for byte, by corpus, each with its reason. A difference
;; not listed, a listed one that differs otherwise (another :why, another first differing line :at, another
;; :as), or a file listed that comes back equal, fails the check; an entry is
;; {"path" {:why :text :at "line N: ..." :reason "..."}}, as -v prints the difference. Not listed, as they are
;; expected: a .cljc read into a .ae comes back as the .cljc, byte for byte (its conditionals
;; recorded at the .ae's end: --full's record, every read's since CDR13 (a), the user 2026-11-22,
;; so :suite-ae and :libs-ae read as :suite-full and :libs-full; before, the one-way rule
;; :reader-conditionals gave back a .clj holding its :clj reading), and from Arbace a text read itself changes (one
;; naming clojure.*), whose printed text makes the round trip from Clojure and whose read-back is
;; exactly what read makes of it. :counts holds each corpus's size, enforced (see run-roundtrip).
{:frozen {}
 :suite-keep-ext {}
 :suite-ae {}
 :libs-keep-ext {}
 :libs-ae {}
 :suite-full {}
 :libs-full {}
 :arbace {}
 ;; the size of each corpus, enforced (audit 076): files read (and so printed back), the .cljc that
 ;; come back as their :clj reading (one-way), the .ae outside read's image (a text read itself
 ;; changes; compared with what read makes of it).
 ;; Measured 2026-11-01 on stage 0, tree of audit-076 (325 files, 175 equal, 150 outside, 0 new):
 ;; bin/repr-clojure roundtrip --from-arbace --known test/repr/clojure/roundtrip-known.edn --corpus arbace arbace
 ;; (150 also under the earlier, weaker condition: the stricter one moved no file).
 ;; Measured again 2026-11-02 on stage 0 after the merges (385 files, 234 equal, 151 outside, 0 new), the
 ;; same command: the 151st repr/c/print.ae (C8's printer), line 434's clojure.core/deref, which read
 ;; itself turns into arbace.core/deref (a text naming clojure.*).
 ;; Measured again 2026-11-08 on stage 0 at mac/next 5ec43f7b (546 files, 394 equal, 152 outside, 0 new), the same
 ;; command: the 152nd genclass.ae (clojure-cdr's CDR3, a4258506f), line 65's comment naming upstream's
 ;; src/clj/clojure/genclass.clj, which read turns into src/clj/arbace/genclass.ae (a text naming clojure.*).
 ;; 2026-11-13 (GTS item 4, branch gate-gts): back to 152. gf-gate's 153rd, repr/asm/arm64/lenc.ae (8744bfdba), defined a private
 ;; `label`, a name arbace.core adds (the Java forms' macro): read's :core-names rule (Clojure source defining a core name Arbace
 ;; adds gets it excluded in its ns form's :refer-clojure) added (:refer-clojure :exclude [label]), which is what made the text
 ;; differ. Neither a reader nor a printer bug: the .ae shadowed arbace.core/label without excluding it; renamed pc-label.
 ;; A change is a reason to look: a corpus that
 ;; emptied or shrank, a file that drifted from equal into an exemption.
 :counts {:frozen {:files 231 :one-way 0 :outside 0}
          :suite-keep-ext {:files 103 :one-way 0 :outside 0}
          :suite-ae {:files 103 :one-way 0 :outside 0}
          :suite-full {:files 103 :one-way 0 :outside 0}
          :libs-keep-ext {:files 33 :one-way 0 :outside 0}
          :libs-ae {:files 33 :one-way 0 :outside 0}
          :libs-full {:files 33 :one-way 0 :outside 0}
          :arbace {:files-min 385 :one-way 0 :outside 152}}} ; arbace/ grows: a floor on the files, the exempted exact
